{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790990615,"nonce":"4RsuaYQN3cvVVu0kG08wRrQRuyc=","title":"Inherit text colour from ancestors, resolved while painting","message":"`\u003cdiv class=\"text-error\"\u003e\u003csvg …\u003e` drew the icon in the default colour, and text the same: an element's colour reached only that element. Text and Svg also bound the theme's primary text colour as their own, which would have blocked inheritance anyway.\n\nashui resolves inheritance in its paint walk (blinc_abi display_list): a node's own text colour wins, otherwise it takes its nearest ancestor's, otherwise the theme's primary text colour (passed in by DisplayList.update, so it follows a scheme transition). Nothing is copied into descendants' props, so content added or recoloured later inherits what its ancestors have then. SVG currentColor is the same inherited colour.\n\nBlinc has the same bug as 9008028 (Stateful-rebuilt content misses inherited CSS) and a second face of it: its stylesheet pass (renderer/stylesheet/base.rs:551, propagate_inherited_text) copies the inherited value into each descendant's own props.text_color, so a later change to the ancestor's colour leaves descendants stale. Proposed to blinc-b1 on 2026-10-03: the same paint-time model. Their fix is tracked in Blinc.","files":null}]}